API key fallback: move to the next API key of a local list when the current credential
runs out of quota, refuse a deny list of models on those keys, and return to the native
credential once its limit has reset. One patch, since each part changes the others' lines.

Rotation. A turn that fails as quota_exhausted (a claude.ai usage limit, or "Credit
balance is too low" from an API key, which the CLI reports as billing_error) marks the
session's credential drained and picks the first key of
~/.config/claude-agent-acp/api-keys not drained yet (CLAUDE_ACP_API_KEYS_FILE
overrides the path; one key per line, # starts a comment). Every session is then
recreated under its id once the active turns settle, with the key as
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY in the query env, and the turn ends normally with a chat line
asking the user to send the message again: JetBrains stops the agent process on a
failed turn, which would take the switch with it. A turn that cannot switch fails
as before. The key also goes in the programmatic settings tier: Claude Code
applies settings.json env after the subprocess env, so a user-level
env.ANTHROPIC_API_KEY would otherwise replace it. Sessions routed by the client
(providers/set, gateway auth) are left alone. A drained key stays drained until the
agent process restarts.

Return. When the native credential runs out, the reset time of the limit, from the
turn's rejected rate_limit_event, is kept with the switch. The first prompt at or
after that time moves every session back to the native credential, recreating them
before the prompt runs. No polling: the time is checked when a prompt arrives. A
limit that reported no reset time, and a key without credit, are never returned
from. A return that is too early costs one round trip: the prompt hits the limit and
switches again.

Deny list. Before a prompt is queued, a session on a key of the list checks its
current model (and the model its alias resolves to, so "default" is caught) against
~/.config/claude-agent-acp/denied-models (CLAUDE_ACP_DENIED_MODELS_FILE overrides
the path; one entry per line in the CLI's deniedModels syntax, so "fable" blocks
the family; # starts a comment), read at each prompt; a missing file denies nothing.
A denied model ends the turn normally with a chat line asking to pick another model,
before any request is sent. The CLI's own deniedModels is read from managed settings
only, which would block the model on the subscription too. Not covered: the
server-side advisor's model, a subagent's own model, and a switch made inside a
running turn.

Each step is a JSON line in ~/.local/state/claude-agent-acp/credential-rotation.log
(CLAUDE_ACP_ROTATION_LOG overrides it), keys shown by their last four characters,
including a session on a key whose init does not report ANTHROPIC_API_KEY as its
key source, a session that cannot be recreated, and a defect in the rotation itself,
which is logged and leaves the quota failure as it was.

Local only, not meant for upstream.

